From e1110ccfdcbc1812315aa63431128392032a5ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kortneythw.tyquisha" <kortneythw.tyquisha@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 04:17:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire shader compilation into the build graph and bake models
 through the cook pipeline

- shaders.manifest.tsv is now the single source of truth for shader builds;
  cmake/ConcordShaders.cmake compiles changed .sc/.sh to embedded SPIR-V
  headers as part of every build (graceful skip when shaderc is absent),
  and build_shaders.ps1 reads the same manifest for manual full rebuilds.
- New CookedModel container ('CMDL'): per-submesh CookedMesh+CookedMaterial
  blobs, bounds and name; deterministic encode, hardened decode.
- concord-cook now imports mesh assets and bakes real CookedModel blobs
  (skinned models stay on the passthrough path for now) via the new
  ConcordImportCore static library (CPU importers, no bgfx).
- New runtime CookedModelSource opens a cooked package (+manifest), verifies
  output hashes and serves parsed models; ModelLoader consults an installed
  cooked source first and falls back to live import on a miss.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
